A solitary figure in a rumpled business suit sits at a pristine hotel window at dusk, back to the viewer, gazing out at an anonymous cityscape of glittering skyscrapers that could be anywhere in Asia. The room is immaculate yet soulless—a perfectly made bed, an open laptop glowing on a desk, an untouched room service tray. The figure's reflection is barely visible in the glass, ghost-like. Outside, warm lights from apartment windows hint at family dinners and connection, contrasting with the cold blue interior light. A single rolling suitcase stands sentinel by the door. The composition emphasizes isolation through negative space and the barrier of glass separating the traveler from the living city below. Rendered in the swirling, emotionally charged brushwork style of Vincent van Gogh, with thick impasto strokes in deep blues and melancholic purples for the interior, while the city beyond pulses with warm yellows and oranges that the traveler cannot reach.
